<title>USA: FSA announces secondary market insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA announces secondary market insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance announces secondary market insurance.</p>
<p>--California State Public Works Board Lease revenue (Dept od Corrections only)</p>
<p>Insurance is available on Maturities 2004 and longer. There is no limit per firm.</p>
<p>FSA has remaining secondary insurance capacity for:</p>
<p>--New York City GO</p>
<p>--New York City Water Finance Authority</p>
<p>--WPPSS</p>
<p>--NYS Med Care (Mental Health)</p>
<p>--Commonwealth of Puerto Rico GO</p>
<p>--Puerto Rico Public Building Authority</p>
<p>Insurance is available on maturities 2005 and longer. There is no par limit per firm.</p>
<p>For futher details, please contact Tom Byrne, Greg Haggerty, or Alan Steinfeld at (212)826-0601.</p>
</text>
